' docs/04_uml/seq_exam_proctoring.puml
@startuml
title Examory - Consented exam proctoring
actor Student
boundary Web
participant "exam-sessions" as Exam
participant webcam as Webcam
participant "Windows client agent" as Agent
participant "event-collector" as Collector
queue Kafka
participant "ML proctoring" as Proctoring
participant grading
actor Teacher

note over Web, grading
  Authenticated APIs use Nginx (omitted). Event payloads and topics
  follow docs/03_architecture/events.md; webcam transport is unspecified.
  Raw video is not embedded in Kafka events.
end note
Student -> Web : Request exam
Web -> Exam : Read session details and consent notice
Exam --> Web : Purpose, webcam/agent collection, retention and withdrawal
Web --> Student : Show separate webcam and agent consent choices
Student -> Web : Submit consent choices
alt Both required consents granted
  Web -> Exam : Record consent flags, version and timestamp
  Exam --> Web : Consent recorded
  Web -> Webcam : Check permission and readiness without capture
  Webcam --> Web : Readiness status
  Web -> Agent : Check connection and readiness without collection
  Agent --> Web : Readiness status
  break Readiness check fails
    Web --> Student : Explain failed check and recovery action; no capture
  end
  Web -> Exam : Start ready, consented session
  Exam --> Web : exam_session_id and active session status
  Exam -> Kafka : exam.started
  note right of Kafka
    Topic: lms.exams.
    Payload: exam_session_id, attempt_id,
    consent {webcam, agent, consent_version, given_at}.
  end note
  Kafka -> Proctoring : exam.started
  Web -> Webcam : Start authorized capture for exam_session_id
  Web -> Agent : Start authorized session monitoring
  loop While ExamSession is active and consent remains valid
    Webcam -> Web : Consented webcam observations
    Web -> Collector : Authorized webcam evidence reference + exam_session_id
    Agent -> Collector : Client signal with exam_session_id
    Collector -> Kafka : exam.agent_signal (authorized signal/evidence references)
    note right of Kafka
      Topic: lms.exams.
      Payload: exam_session_id, signal, details, confidence.
    end note
    Kafka -> Proctoring : exam.agent_signal
    opt Proctoring evaluation reports a risk
      Proctoring -> Kafka : risk.proctoring
      note right of Proctoring
        Topic: ai.risk.
        Payload: risk_id, target_type = exam_session,
        target_id = exam_session_id, score, level,
        model {name, version}, explanation, evidence.
      end note
      Kafka -> grading : risk.proctoring
      grading -> grading : Store risk beside ExamSession; status = pending
    end
  end
  alt Student completes exam
    Web -> Exam : End ExamSession (reason = completed)
  else Server-controlled session time expires
    Exam -> Exam : End ExamSession once (reason = timeout)
  else Student withdraws either consent
    Student -> Web : Withdraw consent and stop monitoring
    Web -> Webcam : Stop capture immediately
    Web -> Agent : Stop collection immediately
    Web -> Exam : Record withdrawal; end ExamSession (reason = withdrawn)
  end
  Exam --> Web : Closed session status
  Web -> Webcam : Ensure capture is stopped
  Web -> Agent : Ensure collection is stopped
  Exam -> Collector : Reject further collection for closed session
  Exam -> Kafka : exam.ended
  note right of Kafka
    Topic: lms.exams.
    Payload: exam_session_id, attempt_id,
    reason = completed | timeout | withdrawn | interrupted,
    ended_at, video_ref.
  end note
  Kafka -> Proctoring : exam.ended; stop session processing
  Web --> Student : Session ended; show completion or withdrawal status
  opt Pending proctoring signals exist
    Teacher -> Web : Inspect pending proctoring signals
    Web -> grading : Read authorized risks and evidence
    grading --> Web : Explanation, evidence and status
    Web --> Teacher : Show review controls
    Teacher -> Web : Confirm or dismiss with reason
    Web -> grading : Save Teacher review
    grading -> Kafka : risk.reviewed
    note right of grading
      Topic: lms.grades.
      Payload: risk_id, target_type, target_id,
      decision = confirmed | dismissed, reviewed_by, comment.
    end note
    grading --> Web : Review saved
  end
else Either required consent declined
  Web --> Student : Session not started; contact Teacher for an alternative
  note over Webcam, Agent : No webcam capture or agent collection starts.
end
note over Exam, grading
  Monitoring failure is shown as unavailable, not proof of misconduct.
  Signal, consent refusal or withdrawal never imposes an automatic penalty.
  Session timeout closes the session independently of Web availability.
  The Agent stops locally on withdrawal or authorization expiry,
  including offline; capture never waits for server acknowledgement.
end note
@enduml
